<figure class="cache-figure" data-cache-circuit>
 <p class="figure-title">An open circuit still needs a bounded fallback</p>
 <p class="figure-note">Five simultaneous callers per burst. Three failed calls open the circuit for 3 s. Half-open permits one probe. Each batch may spend at most two source loads; no queue.</p>
 <div class="circuit-states"><span data-state="closed">Closed<br/><small>Allow cache calls</small></span><span data-state="open">Open<br/><small>Bypass cache calls</small></span><span data-state="half-open">Half-open<br/><small>One probe</small></span></div>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Redis outcome <select data-outcome aria-label="Redis request outcome"><option value="failure">Connection fails</option><option value="miss">Successful miss</option><option value="hit">Cache hit</option></select></label><button data-action="burst">Send five requests</button><button data-action="advance">Advance 3 seconds</button><button data-action="probe">Finish probe</button><button data-reset>Reset</button></div>
 <div class="circuit-callers" data-callers></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Clock: <b data-now>0 s</b> · Redis attempts: <b data-attempts>0</b> · probe: <b data-probe>none</b></p>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Send a failing burst, then another while open. Advance the clock and send again to start one probe; another burst cannot start a second. Select Successful miss and finish the probe. The circuit closes even though that answer needs source work. Each burst is a separate admission-budget illustration, not a production rate limiter. Earlier batches disappear; a pending probe remains tracked.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {breakerInitial,breakerStep} from '../../lib/caching/failures.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-circuit]').forEach(root=>{let s=breakerInitial();const outcome=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-outcome]')!;const names={source:'Source admitted',rejected:'Fallback refused',hit:'Cache answer',probe:'Probe pending'};const render=()=>{root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-state]').forEach(el=>el.classList.toggle('active',el.dataset.state===s.mode));root.querySelector('[data-callers]')!.replaceChildren(...s.rows.map(row=>{const el=document.createElement('div');el.className=row.result;const label=document.createElement('b');label.textContent=`Caller ${row.id}`;const route=document.createElement('small');route.textContent=row.route;const result=document.createElement('span');result.textContent=names[row.result as keyof typeof names];el.append(label,route,result);return el;}));for(const [name,value]of Object.entries({now:`${s.now} s`,attempts:String(s.attempts),probe:s.probe?'one in flight':s.lastProbe==='none'?'none':`last finished: ${names[s.lastProbe as keyof typeof names]}`,explanation:s.message}))root.querySelector(`[data-${name}]`)!.textContent=value;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-action="probe"]')!.disabled=!s.probe;};root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-action]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{s=breakerStep(s,b.dataset.action!,outcome.value);render();});root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.onclick=()=>{s=breakerInitial();outcome.value='failure';render();};render();});
</script>
